+
+no-split alternative:
+  conditional Prop-6.3 descent to (24,16; M2'=18,V2'=7;k=4)
+  promoted status pending exact compiler audit / support-map gate
+
+overall D=108 row:
+  no REPRESENTATIVE; no recomposed pair; no JC2 counterexample.
+```
+
+The second client does not uniformise by reusing only the late pole/Jacobian
+schedule. At `(99,66)`, the charged branches first became unit at stage 4
+(Jacobian row `6264`) and stage 8 (pole row `64`), as recorded in
+`g9966-delta52-stage8-sol56-20260903.md:160-172`. Here the branch-specific
+common-`h3` incidence kills before either family is reached. A uniform engine
+therefore needs a parameterized **incidence compiler and exact Q-star reducer**
+ahead of a shared continuation scheduler; the latter alone misses the row
+family that decides this client.
+
+## 11. Reproduction index
+
+Primary boxed files:
+
+```text
+box/g108band-20260903/band_engine.py
+box/g108band-20260903/outer_order_bands.py
+box/g108band-20260903/controls.py
+box/g108band-20260903/descent_engine.py
+box/g108band-20260903/outer-bands.json
