@@ -0,0 +1,518 @@
+# `D = 108` joint-chart band engine (packet Q3)
+
+Status: **COMPLETE BODY — UNSEALED PENDING FINAL VALIDATION**
+
+## 0. Result first
+
+The unique split branch is
+
+```text
+delta = 3, partition [1,1]
+p = pi^2-c, c != 0
+q = p^23 U, dU/dpi = 5p^2, deg U = 5
+one modulus e0 after translation/scaling gauge
+24 principal G-roots -> 12+12, both final at delta' = 4.
+```
+
+The exact joint-chart compiler kills it at **stage 0 preflight**, before a
+direct `F/G` pole row or Jacobian row is reached. Seven rational `Q*` pivots
+in the common-`h3` incidence leave five normal forms; with the declared
+Rabinowitsch equation `Zc*c-1`, their ideal contains `1`. Characteristic-zero
+Singular returns dimension `-1`, standard basis `1`, normal form of `1` equal
+to `0`, and the same explicit lift certificate. The split verdict is
+
+```text
+DEAD[D108 / delta=3 / DECLARED-NECESSARY-JOINT-CHART]
+killing family = common-h3 minor incidence
+first unit stage = 0 preflight
+```
+
+No `F,G` pair is recomposed, and no `REPRESENTATIVE` is claimed. The no-split
+alternative is conditional on `delta* >= 7/2`; Proposition 6.3 applies directly
+and descends to `(24,16)`. Its exact promoted status is recorded separately in
+§7 because the denominator-shed support/ring map must not be supplied by
+analogy.
+
+## 1. Custody, scope, and execution contract
+
+The lane receipt `xmodel/g108-joint-band-sol56-20260903.run.v2` declares 18
+frozen inputs under `/tmp/jc2-lane.BhSYQx/inputs`. The manifest was generated
+mechanically from its `charged_input_<i>_sha256` and
+`charged_input_<i>_basename` fields and then passed to `sha256sum -c`; all 18
+lines returned `OK`. No digest was retyped. The stage-0 manifest SHA-256 is
+`530034c276bc8e84b9a3d4a3078d023d6d13d61bd8547c2172091784567d60a7`.
+
+The charged classification gives the datum and unique branch at
+`g108-minor-classification-opus5-20260903.md:4-26`, the rigid `12+12` tree at
+`:201-215`, and the split/no-split dichotomy at `:222-238`. It gives the tower,
+ambient counts, local leaders, and Jacobian scalars at `:240-301`, while
+explicitly leaving the new weight cuts, equality table, `D1` boundary, outer
+offsets, and pole schedule for this lane at `:303-326`. Thus every number that
+was `OPEN[108-OUTER-WEIGHTS]` is derived here, not copied by analogy.
+
+All engine invocations were foreground processes of the form
+
+```text
+timeout 3000 taskset -c 0-3 env \
+  OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 MKL_NUM_THREADS=1 \
+  NUMEXPR_NUM_THREADS=1 /usr/bin/time -v python3 DRIVER ...
+```
+
+The machine exposed CPUs `0-15`; the recorded process affinity was `0-3`.
+Software was Python 3.12.3, SymPy 1.12, and Singular 4.3.2. No background job
+was launched. Writes are bounded to `box/g108band-20260903/` and this report;
+there are no ledger, `jc2-lean`, `ideation-*`, or prohibited lane-report edits.
+
+## 2. Datum, tower, and conventions
+
+The input row is
+
+```text
+(n,m) = (108,72)
+M = (-72,81,106), d = (108,36,9,1), V = (7,7)
+u3 = 2, v3 = 7; major radii = (3/8,1/4,-1).
+```
+
+The fixed orientation is `F=degree 108`, `G=degree 72`. It is the opposite of
+the historical lower-case `(f,g)` order in some source passages. The
+Tschirnhausen tower is
+
+```text
+h3 = P,                                  deg_y 9,   top P=y^2(y-x)^7
+h2 = P^4 + C2 P^2 + C3 P + C4,          deg_y 36
+F  = h2^3 + A2 h2 + A3,                 deg_y 108
+G  = h2^2 + B1 h2 + B2.                 deg_y 72
+```
+
+Set `z=w-1`,
+
+```text
+K3(t,w)=t^9 h3(t^-1,w/t),
+K2(t,w)=t^36 h2(t^-1,w/t).
+```
+
+At the major `D2` node, `t=s^4`, `z=pi*s^6`; hence the weight is
+`4r+6q`, or primitive weight `W=2r+3q`. At `D1`, `s=e^2`, so
+`t=e^8`, `z=e^12(1+Pi*e)`. This is the charged §3 convention
+(`g108-minor-classification...md:320-325`). Replacing it by `4r+5q` would
+identify the major flag coordinate with the later physical minor series; that
+is precisely the flag/place/series conflation barred by FALLACY-v2. The two
+maps are declared separately below.
+
+The raw block counts are
+
+| block | H | C2 | C3 | C4 | A2 | A3 | B1 | B2 | total |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| raw monic chart | 54 | 135 | 216 | 297 | 1998 | 3294 | 702 | 1998 | 8694 |
+| after fixed tops | 45 | 126 | 207 | 288 | 1962 | 3258 | 666 | 1962 | **8514** |
+
+The branch parameters are named `jet1,jet2,c,e0`. Here `U(pi)` is the
+degree-five factor in `q=p^23 U`; it is never called `u`, so it cannot be
+confused with a jet coefficient or with `u3=2`. The modulus `e0` belongs to
+the effective-root face and does not enter the necessary common-`h3` block.
+No unproved effective-`T2/T3` bridge identifies it with an `F,G` coefficient.
+
+## 3. Exact adaptation map from `(99,66)`
+
+| charged engine item | `D=108` replacement |
+|---|---|
+| old receipt/frozen directory, 20 inputs | this receipt, `/tmp/jc2-lane.BhSYQx/inputs`, 18 inputs |
+| two branches `delta2`, `delta52` | one branch `delta3`; no `mu_2` equivariance because `e=1` |
+| degrees `99/66`, tower `11 subset 33` | degrees `108/72`, tower `9 subset 36` |
+| `K3` top `z^8(1+z)^3` | `z^7(1+z)^2` |
+| `h3` cap `11-r`, 21 strict coordinates | cap `9-r`, 7 strict coordinates |
+| `h2=h3^3+C2*h3+C3` | `h2=h3^4+C2*h3^2+C3*h3+C4` |
+| post-`h3` ambient `516` | post-`h3` ambient **628** |
+| major weight `3r+4q` | `4r+6q`, primitive `2r+3q` |
+| `D1`: `t=e^9`, `z=e^12(1+Pi*e)` | `t=e^8`, `z=e^12(1+Pi*e)` |
+| `K2` face `(pi^3-1)^8`; 7 `D1` rows | `pi^12(pi^2-1)^8`; 4 `D1` rows |
+| `build_FG`: cube/square in `K2` | unchanged because `n/d2=3`, `m/d2=2` |
+| fixed outer degrees `65/98/32/65` | **`71/107/35/71`**, not raw slot degrees `72/108/36/72` |
+| outer `D2` rank 5598, `D1` rank 176 | ranks **7656** and **54** |
+| local centers for orders `2`, `5/2` | `w=jet1*t^2+jet2*t^3+pi*t^4` for order `3` |
+| pole normalizers/shifts branch-dependent | `F: pole 12, shift 96`; `G: pole 8, shift 64` |
+| Jacobian scalars `99,-66`, top degree 163 | `108,-72`, top degree 178 |
+| already-solved hard-coded `h3_branch_map` | construct incidence rows first; otherwise the decisive residue is erased |
+| all positive-degree Jacobian targets zero | additionally subtract `1` at degree zero |
+| legacy “nonlinear residue appears” boolean | distinguish zero, rational unit, and genuine nonlinear residue |
+
+The raw outer numbers in the charged D=108 design table are slot degrees.
+Using them directly would be an off-by-one error: after fixing each top face,
+the coefficient supports have degrees `71,107,35,71`. The source-compatible
+driver records this correction explicitly.
+
+## 4. Theorem-1.2 and outer ranks
+
+### 4.1 Major `h3` and the 628 analogue
+
+The fixed-top `H` block has 45 lower coordinates. Relative to boundary
+`4r+6q=42`, 36 are strictly below and two are unwanted at-level sites
+`(3,5),(6,3)`. These are 36 order rows plus two separate face-incidence rows,
+not an undifferentiated count. Rank is `38`; the seven strict coordinates are
+
+```text
+Hc_1_7 Hc_1_8 Hc_2_6 Hc_2_7 Hc_3_6 Hc_4_5 Hc_5_4.
+```
+
+Consequently the requested 516-analogue is
+
+```text
+H 7 + C2 126 + C3 207 + C4 288 = 628.
+```
+
+The `K2` boundary is `168`. Exactly 558 projected positions lie strictly
+below it and eight are at level:
+
+```text
+(r,q)=(3k,28-2k), 1<=k<=8,
+value=(-1)^k binom(8,k).
+```
+
+These encode `pi^12(pi^2-1)^8`. Among the nominal `558+8=566` labels,
+`(1,27)` is an exact approximate-root identity. The other 565 rows form a
+unit-triangular block:
+
+| leader block | output q-range | exact pivots |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| C4 | 0..8 | 288 |
+| C3 (times top q=9 of `h3`) | 9..17 | 198 |
+| C2 (times top q=18 of `h3^2`) | 18..26 | 79 |
+| total | | **565** |
+
+Thus `628-565=63`. At `D1`, the face begins at `e^344`; only primitive
+weight `W=85` contributes below it, at `e^340,...,e^343`. The four binomial
+rows have rank four. Columns with `q=(25,23,21,19)` give determinant `64`.
+The exact inner ledger is therefore
+
+```text
+fixed inner ambient                                      666
+h3: strict order 36 + face 2, rank                       38
