+The two points `[1:-a:0]` and `[1:1-a:0]` are distinct, their coordinate
+difference being `-1`. The shared linear ansatz produces only
+`A-C-1`; the slice `(A,C)=(2,1)` gives `(2x+y,x+y)` with Jacobian one. All
+symbolic inverse, factorization, determinant, incidence, and witness checks
