+## 8. Controls
+
+### 8.1 `(64,48) -> (16,12)` Appendix II
+
+The driver mechanically obtains `d=(64,16,4,2)`, `d_s=4`, `v_s=3`, `u_s=1`
+and hence `(64,48)/4=(16,12)`. It builds both readings of Moh p.208: the
+printed repeated `c5` and the compiler's absorbed-`alpha1`, distinct-`c6`
+reading. Each has 17 coefficient variables and 77 coefficients of the
+Jacobian equation. Exact-Q Singular with `Zc*c-1` returns dimension `-1` and
+basis `1` for both. The raw ideal is nonunit; empty, point, and lift controls
+all pass. Foreground wall time was 1:03.83 and peak RSS 520,888 KiB.
+
+This reproduces the Appendix-II kill in characteristic zero, stronger than the
+frozen modular calibration. The control's ordered Jacobian is the negative of
+the main engine orientation; localization of the otherwise free nonzero scalar
+makes the sign harmless and the convention is recorded.
