+The two points `[1:-a:0]` and `[1:1-a:0]` are distinct, their coordinate
+difference being `-1`. The shared linear ansatz produces only
+`A-C-1`; the slice `(A,C)=(2,1)` gives `(2x+y,x+y)` with Jacobian one. All
+symbolic inverse, factorization, determinant, incidence, and witness checks
+pass. The special `D=108` tower rows are correctly marked not applicable to
+degrees `(1,1)`.
+
+## 9. FALLACY-v2 audit
+
+- **Flag/place/series:** the major `D2/D1` maps, physical minor series, split
+  order `delta=3`, combined radius `delta*`, and denominator shedding are all
+  separately declared. Strict-below rows and at-level face rows have separate
+  counts.
+- **Charge/carrier/attainment:** no new exit-price assertion is made, so no
+  `charge_basis` declaration is licensed. A screen survivor is not treated as
+  an actual exit, and no lower bound is promoted to attainment.
+- **Pole/interior:** pole and Jacobian schedules are unreachable metadata; the
+  death uses only the necessary common-`h3` incidence, so no interior identity
+  is invoked after a missing hypothesis.
+- **Localization:** the ideal component is displayed in
+  `Q[jet1,jet2,c,Zc]`, `c` is excluded from rational pivots, `Zc*c-1` is
+  explicit, and raw/empty/point controls plus a unit lift are run.
+- **Remainders and maps:** zero rows are counted; the correct scalar sign is
+  checked; the five nonzero normal forms are displayed. `e0` is not mapped by
+  name to an `F,G` coordinate. Prime marks in descended data are labels;
+  `dU/dpi` is written explicitly when differentiation is meant.
+- **Descent:** Proposition 6.3 is used only on the stated no-split premise.
+  Proposition 6.4 is not substituted. The missing ordinary-support map is
+  typed `OPEN`, rather than filled by a cap or analogy.
+- **Merge/arrival:** no merge-free or arrival-index claim is made in this lane.
+
+## 10. Verdict and uniformisation evidence
+
+```text
+split alternative:
+  DEAD[D108/delta3/DECLARED-NECESSARY-JOINT-CHART]
+  exact stage = 0 preflight
+  killing family = common-h3 minor incidence
+  certificate = localized unit ideal over Q
+
+no-split alternative:
+  conditional Prop-6.3 descent to (24,16; M2'=18,V2'=7;k=4)
+  charged compiler diagnostic DEAD (26 rows, exact Q)
+  promoted status OPEN[DESCENT-SUPPORT/VARIABLE-MAP]
+
+overall D=108 row:
+  no REPRESENTATIVE; no recomposed pair; no JC2 counterexample.
+```
+
+The second client does not uniformise by reusing only the late pole/Jacobian
+schedule. At `(99,66)`, the charged branches first became unit at stage 4
+(Jacobian row `6264`) and stage 8 (pole row `64`), as recorded in
+`g9966-delta52-stage8-sol56-20260903.md:160-172`. Here the branch-specific
+common-`h3` incidence kills before either family is reached. A uniform engine
+therefore needs a parameterized **incidence compiler and exact Q-star reducer**
+ahead of a shared continuation scheduler; the latter alone misses the row
+family that decides this client.
+
+## 11. Reproduction index
+
