+## 8. Controls
+
+### 8.1 `(64,48) -> (16,12)` Appendix II
+
+The driver mechanically obtains `d=(64,16,4,2)`, `d_s=4`, `v_s=3`, `u_s=1`
+and hence `(64,48)/4=(16,12)`. It builds both readings of Moh p.208: the
